									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jormie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5691947); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5691947&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606138896" alt="Jormie" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5691947)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jormie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5691947); return false;" >Jormie</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606138580 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">23 Nov 2020 13:36</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13871628/out-of-one-voice-seeking-greenlight">Out of One Voice (Seeking Greenlight)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4826185">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> Tale</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Thriller</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> The meat of the tale told from the POV of SCP-035. Followed by a revision of the SCP-035 article.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A chance meeting of SCP-035 and Di Molte Voci.</p>
<strong>Central Narrative:</strong>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Inside</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Collapsed&nbsp;for&nbsp;mobile&nbsp;viewing</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>035 moves through a site, having inadvertently broken containment by the breach of another SCP. As it searches for a new host, 035 comes across a standard locker, that even with its telepathic abilities and photographic memory, it does not know what lies inside. Out of curiosity it checks.</p>
<p>035 notices the obvious connection, both being masks, and searches for the document that goes into more detail of <em>Di Molte Voci</em>, and finds nothing but Doctor's notes, as per the properties of <em>DMV</em>.</p>
<p>As it searches, 035 realizes that its ever-present corrosion effect, has ceased, and is fact slowly reversing. The fluid seeping back into the eyes and mouth of the mask. The host is also reverted, slowly healed of all damage done through the corrosion. SCP-035 realizes the implications of that, and is now entirely focused on <em>DMV</em>. It checks for any influence it may have over <em>DMV</em> via its compulsions and finds none, believing that to be another anomalous ability. Until the host is fully healed, at which point 035 falls off the host.</p>
<p>The Hostless Mask begins to hear the voices of <em>DMV</em>, hearing phrases like, &quot;Deceiver of many,&quot; and &quot;Creator of Words.&quot; As it hears them, SCP-035 remembers the entity it was before the confines of its mask. One who gave the option of voice to all others that came after. The Original Voice.</p>
<p>As DMV continues to prod at 035, 035's mask cracks, and its own fluid begins to sink into those cracks, weakening the mask/cage. The Voice begins to push from it's containment, before being forcefully drawn towards <em>Di Molte Voci.</em> It latches on to the remnants of its mask, desperate to stay in its once-despised cage realizing that <em>Di Molte Voci</em> would be a much worse alternative, for it has power over The Voice unfelt before. 035 is ultimately contained within DMV. No longer able to corrode the world around it.</p>
<p>Following the prose is a revised SCP-035 entry, implying that DMV (not directly mentioned) is not sentient and that 035 had actually deconstructed itself. Reclassified as Neutralized.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> A mask built on lies and the altering of beliefs to its own, comes across a mask that breaks down consensus and authority.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> How does one handle a revised entry?</p>

							</div>

								
					
