<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-XXXX</p>
<p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid</p>
<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong>SCP-XXXX must be contained in a 10m x 10m reinforced concrete and steel chamber, the cell must be shined with standard light bulbs at all times and spotlights in the outer cell to prevent containment breach. If a light bulb is broken, three D-class personnel (no more, no less) must enter the cell with the cell doors closed behind them. One D-class must hold a flashlight towards SCP-XXXX while the other two D-class personnel can safely repair the light bulb.</p>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-XXXX appears to be an old broken statue that was dated back to the mid-7th century BCE with an unknown origin, the object has a missing left elbow, the right arm seems to be intact, and holds a broken hilt. The object's face seems to be broken as well the face is missing a nose and a right ear. It stands over 7 feet and SCP-XXXX has a thick baseplate underneath that is measured to be 11 centimeters thick and has a chiseled title called &quot;A Stone Heart&quot;, its weight was measured to be over 700 kilograms. SCP-XXXX have signs that tools were used to make SCP-XXXX, SCP-XXXX was chiseled from black andesite.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX is hostile towards any human victims, SCP-XXXX cannot move when light touches the object, depending on its brightness. When light is removed from SCP-XXXX, the object anomalously moves towards the nearest subject, its speed depends on how dark the environment or containment it is in. Personnel reported noises of chiseling rocks created by SCP-XXXX when it moves its torso, head, or arms. When SCP-XXXX is close to its victim, SCP-XXXX will strike the victim's head with either its arm or its broken hilt with great force and speed. Testings on SCP-XXXX's movements were approved.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Testing 12 lumen (Candle light) - 7/██/██</strong></span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Subject:</strong> D-32794</p>
<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> D-class personnel was instructed to stand in a corner, the light in the containment changed to 12 lumens equivalent to wax candlelight.</p>
<p><strong>Results:</strong> SCP-XXXX moves towards D-32794 slowly, at about 1kmph. D-32794 walks backward as she locks eye contact with SCP-XXXX movements.</p>
<p><strong>Analysis:</strong> This was an interesting SCP, its movement depends highly on the light.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Testing 1 lumen (Moonlight) - 7/██/██</strong></span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Subject:</strong> D-32794</p>
<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> D-class personnel was instructed to stand in a corner as last time, the light in the containment changes to 1-lumen equivalent to moonlight.</p>
<p><strong>Results:</strong> SCP-XXXX moves towards D-32794 with unbelievable speeds, SCP-XXXX kills D-32794 with the broken hilt.</p>
<p><strong>Analysis:</strong> The speeds were calculated to be 70kmph after testing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Testing (Complete Darkness) - █/██/██</strong></span></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Subject:</strong> D-23932</p>
<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> D-class personnel were instructed to stand in a corner same as the last two tests, the containment's light turns off.</p>
<p><strong>Results:</strong> As the lights turned off, the sound of a skull-cracking was heard in the SCP-XXXX containment cell. D-23932 was instantly killed after approximately 2 seconds when the lights turned off.</p>
<p><strong>Analysis:</strong> Not only SCP-XXXX proved itself dangerous, but also unpredictable in its nature. Thus it's SCP-XXXX has classed into a Euclid class.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
